  "details": "I have a public avatar favorited that I clearly remember has animations that activate with hand gestures.\nSince (most likely) build 1088/2021.2.1, which introduced a lot of changes to avatar loading, I can not use any of these, in either VR or on desktop mode.\nExample avatar: avtr_6626d8cd-7de8-4858-af35-63d56d67c381\nI haven't used that avatar in a while, so I can't remember which hand gestures activate animations, but it could:\n1. hide in a pot,\n2. extend out of a pot,\n3. chirp once while opening it's beak.\n\nAdditional thing I noticed is that if you are in VR, is that upon switching to any generic rigged avatar, you will see your controllers and optionally tracker spheres, as if you were supposed to calibrate to it, but pressing both triggers doesn't do anything.\nThis is further confirmed by the fact that opening any of the big menus (like Settings, Social etc.) will cause them to disappear, which is exactly the same behavior as if during FBT calibration.\n\nEmotes are NOT affected by this, they work completely fine.\n\nProbably related bug happening only on Open Beta: https://vrchat.canny.io/open-beta/p/1104-with-fbt-active-generic-avatars-appear-below-the-floor-locally",
